course: dictionary
lesson: 10984
title: Warn: telling someone about danger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To warn someone means to tell them about a danger or problem before it happens, so they can be careful or avoid it. Warn is a verb: warn, warns, warned, warning. A warning is the signal or message itself.
explain: Look at «A dog that growls, shows its teeth or goes stiff is warning you to stay away.» The growl, the teeth and the stiff body all come before any bite. They tell you about danger before it happens, so you keep away. That is a warning.
explain: Warn can also mean to strongly advise someone to do or not do something, as in «warn someone not to» touch the hot pan. Clue words such as about, not to, or what will happen tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Look at «A skunk... usually warns first by stamping, hissing and raising its tail.» The words warns first tell you the warning comes before the spray. Ask yourself: is this a warning before trouble, or the trouble itself?
fact: To warn means to tell someone about a danger or problem before it happens.
fact: A warning is the signal or message that does this, such as a yellow warning triangle or a «Danger» sign.
fact: «Warn» can also mean to tell someone what will happen if they keep doing something wrong.
fact: In nature, bright colours can warn that an animal is poisonous, like the stripes of a wasp.
fact: Useful phrases: warn someone about, warn someone not to, warning sign, without warning, a final warning.
exercise: «A dog that growls, shows its teeth or goes stiff is warning you to stay away.» What does warning mean here? | Asking you to come closer | Playing a game with you | *Telling you about danger so you keep away | Going to sleep
exercise: Which of these is a warning sign? | A birthday cake | A smiling face | *A yellow triangle with «Danger» on it | A library book
exercise: «A skunk... usually warns first by stamping, hissing and raising its tail.» Find and copy the word that shows the warning comes before the spray. | *first | skunk | tail | smelly
test: Which of these tells people about danger before it happens? | *A fire alarm that sounds when there is smoke | A slow song | A birthday card
test: What does «warn someone not to» mean? | Give them a present | Tell them a joke | *Strongly advise them not to do something | Ask them to sing
exam: In «A dog warns before it bites: it yawns, licks its lips, turns its head away», what does warns mean? | Bites harder and faster | Sleeps soundly in the sun | Runs away quickly | *Gives signs of danger before it bites
